[agent:result] === job deploy ===
[agent:result] Usage: hops job deploy [OPTIONS] NAME SCRIPT
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Deploy a job end to end: upload, set environment, schedule, run.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   One-shot for what ``create`` + ``schedule`` + ``run`` do separately, plus
[agent:result]   the environment selection that ``create`` cannot set. ``SCRIPT`` is either a
[agent:result]   local file (uploaded to HopsFS) or an existing HopsFS path.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Args:     ctx: Click context.     name: Job name (created or updated).
[agent:result]   script: Local file to upload, or an existing HopsFS path.     job_type: One
[agent:result]   of PYTHON/PYSPARK/SPARK/DOCKER.     environment: Python environment name;
[agent:result]   the type default if omitted.     app_args: Argument string passed to the
[agent:result]   job.     cron: Schedule; Quartz or a shorthand. No schedule if omitted.
[agent:result]   do_run: Run once after deploying.     wait: With ``do_run``, block until the
[agent:result]   execution terminates.     upload_dir: HopsFS directory for a local script
[agent:result]   upload.     overwrite: Overwrite an existing uploaded script.
